# Workflow tool e2e: the model writes a Lua orchestration script that
# fans out two parallel subagents (zag.workflow.parallel + zag.task),
# each shelling out for a deterministic token, and returns the joined
# results. Exercises the whole dynamic-workflow stack end to end:
# script execution on the main-thread coroutine, child AgentRunner
# spawn/drain, borrowed-pane rendering, and result marshaling back into
# the parent turn.
#
# Anchoring: the prompt names only REVERSED seeds; each child must
# `rev` its seed via bash, so the waited tokens can only originate in
# child tool output surfacing through the workflow result.

spawn ./zig-out/bin/zag
wait_text /Welcome to zag/
wait_idle 500ms
send "Use the workflow tool. The Lua script must call zag.workflow.parallel with two functions: the first runs zag.task with the prompt: run bash echo 7R-A-fw-gaz | rev and reply with only its stdout; it returns task.summary. The second is identical but with 4K-B-fw-gaz. parallel returns one slot per function shaped {value=..., err=...}, so the script must end with: return slots[1].value .. ' ' .. slots[2].value. After the tool finishes, repeat its result verbatim." <Enter>
# Parent turn + two child turns: give the fan-out a generous deadline.
wait_text /zag-wf-A-R7/ 180s
wait_text /zag-wf-B-K4/ 30s
# Let the parent turn finish streaming before quitting.
wait_idle 2s 60s
snapshot final
send "/quit" <Enter>
wait_exit 30s
